course: dictionary
lesson: 9917
title: Tamp: pressing down and calming down
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tamp is a verb, and it has two meanings. The main one is to press something down firmly so it is packed tight. Gardeners do this: «After planting the seedling, tamp down the soil gently so the plant stands firm.»
explain: Look at the words around tamp to find its meaning. Soil, plant, stands firm and packed tight are clues that tamp means pressing. Try the swap: "press down the soil gently" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Tamp also has a formal meaning: to calm or reduce something, such as feelings or rumours. In news writing, «to tamp down fears» means to calm worries. Clues like fears and rumours tell you that nothing is being pressed flat here.
fact: Tamp means to press or pat something down firmly so it is packed tight.
fact: Gardeners tamp the soil around a plant so that it stands firm.
fact: Builders tamp down gravel or concrete to make a hard, level surface.
fact: In a café, a barista tamps the coffee in the machine before the water goes through it.
fact: Formal use: «tamp down» can mean to calm or reduce something, such as fears or rumours.
exercise: «After planting the seedling, you tamp down the soil gently.» What does tamp down mean here? | Dig a deep hole | *Press the soil down firmly | Pull the plant out | Water it until it runs away
exercise: Builders «tamp down the gravel» before they pour the concrete. What are they doing? | Throwing the gravel away | *Pressing the gravel down so it is packed tight | Painting the gravel bright colours | Melting the gravel
exercise: «The head teacher wanted to tamp down the rumours.» What does tamp down suggest? | *Calm the rumours and reduce them | Write the rumours in a book | Shout the rumours out loud | Make the rumours spread quickly
test: In a café, a barista tamps the coffee in the machine. What is the barista doing? | Pouring water through it | *Pressing it down firmly so it is packed tight | Stirring it fast with a spoon | Throwing it out
test: Which phrase is the best swap for «tamp down fears»? | Write the fears down | Hide the fears in a box | Make the fears bigger | *Calm the worries
exam: Which phrase uses tamp in its formal sense? | Tamp the soil firm | Tamp the coffee | *Tamp down the rumours | Tamp it firm around the stem
